.TH tustate n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tustate
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBstateDiagram\fR / \fBstateDiagram\-v2\fR block into a \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR model, so a state diagram can render natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine — no browser. It is one of the graph\-type parsers the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade dispatches to; you normally call \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR rather than this module directly.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tustate 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tustate::parse text      ;# -> tudiagram model dict
.CE
.PP
The result is a \fBtudiagram\fR model and is rendered with \fBtclutils::tudiagram::toSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR (or via the \fBtuflow\fR facade).
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
states           -> rounded boxes
transitions      -> edges:  A --> B   (optional ": label")
[*]              -> start (__start) / end (__end) marker, by side
"S : text"       -> sets state S's display label
state X <<fork>> -> a labelled box named X (also <<join>>)
direction LR|RL|TB|TD|BT  -> layout direction (RL->LR, BT/TD->TB)
.CE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tustate
package require tclutils::tudiagram

set src {stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Running : start
    Running --> Idle : stop
    Running --> [*]
}
set m [::tclutils::tustate::parse $src]
::tclutils::tudiagram::writePng $m state.png -scale 3
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
v1 limitations (honest): composite states \fBstate X { ... }\fR are flattened (inner transitions kept, the boundary box is not drawn); notes are ignored; fork/join render as boxes, not bars; self\-loops are not drawn.
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (renderer), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUSTATE <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no states/transitions found).
